# Claude Code's working directory, ALL of it. This repo is public, and
# nothing under .claude/ is of any use to someone who clones it: it is
# this machine's agent setup — IDEA Base project/task ids, the hub-and-
# spoke tab topology, which models we pay for and why, bypassPermissions
# as a house default, and symlink paths into ~/.claude/projects. None of
# that describes ConsoleForge the product.
#
# .claude/commands/start.md used to be tracked on the reasoning that "a
# spoke cannot read a file that only exists on the hub's disk". True, and
# it does not follow: a spoke is launched by consoleforge-tab on THIS
# machine, so user scope (~/.claude/commands/) reaches it just as well
# without publishing our operations to every cloner. Ignore the whole
# directory rather than naming files, so the next command added here does
# not leak the same way.
.claude/
